17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316395} {:answer/id #uuid "f14c58f5-1028-5c49-9498-4fa870884bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f8c86b-97a6-5594-83dd-cfdf53dd65e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315866} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e07b27-e561-5526-8490-7c4c7c666936" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c42f52e-06bd-52e2-95d3-14aef2760932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315190} {:answer/id #uuid "916b8837-a7c4-518a-8c62-6b08a8d8b906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315929} {:answer/id #uuid "b4da5379-6c12-542e-abc1-899c39aec7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316141} {:answer/id #uuid "ea796d2d-091a-5239-843e-5556c9bc8def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea796d2d-091a-5239-843e-5556c9bc8def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316421} :answer-field/id #uuid "c28a283a-279e-5531-8559-3c90d0e4d547" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60f30b7a-ba21-59d7-b0c6-278dc23eb425" :question/math-academy-id "q-343063" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-(-2))+3Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4})-3(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}) \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)+2 & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, subtract $2$ from the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-2 \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{2({s}^{2}+4)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+3)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+4),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n-2{s}^{2}-3s-4=A({s}^{2}+4)+(Bs+C)(s+3)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-2(-3)^{2}-3(-3)-4=A((-3)^{2}+4)+0\\,⟹\\,-13=13A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n-2=A+B\\,⟹\\,-2=-1+B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n-4=4A+3C\\,⟹\\,-4=4(-1)+3C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{-s}{{s}^{2}+4}=-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ec5f87f-9270-584d-aa85-8ec2245ee243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec5f87f-9270-584d-aa85-8ec2245ee243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315569} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24554c4-5641-57c6-a274-4ab338fde6ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "224166c5-b66f-5ed1-bc58-63e5ea30c6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-343160" :question/problem "The number of views $V,$ in millions, of a viral video after $t$ days is modeled by $V(t)=\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}$ for $0\\le t\\le 6.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} views per day." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is equal to ${V}^{′}(t).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{10}^{t}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10} \\\\  & ={10}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is ${10}^{t}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "352a4a98-711e-5daf-a9a7-cb6c59b4a6a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352a4a98-711e-5daf-a9a7-cb6c59b4a6a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315428} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7b5b25-9f87-565d-bb02-622c4b9fbc38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1c4a7f6-dfa8-527f-a427-71639bc74bac" :question/math-academy-id "q-343173" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\frac{7}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6-x))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6-x):$ \n\n![](images/04/04dd8257ef32291b930aa29f5bed4de2c41761692fd48d08ed2479f6cbd78659.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6-x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6-x)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\frac{7}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6-x))=\\frac{7}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7baa51a-91a1-5787-bc67-a1f0ff0f3e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7baa51a-91a1-5787-bc67-a1f0ff0f3e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316322} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9e6a31-e2dd-5d07-852e-47b2fce10fea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fff73ba7-51c3-55f6-9993-4fc2cbedd36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343215" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+x)$ at $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+x)] \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(1+x)^{2}}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-(1+2x+{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2x-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2(-1)-(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "102c20a7-364b-5e1d-8e5b-1a8f7adb1463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315216} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4a5b80-b993-5acb-b1fc-0027ff1b76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315921} {:answer/id #uuid "9bfc4594-abfa-5c41-b497-cf307852b689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f4a5b80-b993-5acb-b1fc-0027ff1b76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315921} :answer-field/id #uuid "5244a3bb-594f-53ba-b2ef-f72d466a2fc7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226b5654-77e7-5290-83cb-1a0492f45274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{252(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315307} {:answer/id #uuid "60c3bc85-544e-5b9f-ab33-7b566e41ce0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315659} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5f4e68-ccd2-570b-9ee9-e4c567858d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{252(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315810} {:answer/id #uuid "a9af117d-edd7-5efb-8dba-c537f16eed90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9af117d-edd7-5efb-8dba-c537f16eed90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316072} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5d328c-5ae8-55b6-b9ab-a3f56bbb2e90" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288201e6-f2dd-5dfd-bddb-d01ad4149311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315351} {:answer/id #uuid "9c12c233-b887-55fa-88ba-f3727f0b1a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "288201e6-f2dd-5dfd-bddb-d01ad4149311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315351} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3026fce-a564-560d-a98f-f8c84ca4478f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b4c586-dd65-581f-b72e-da973be223dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise linear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315664} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a765d5-f9bc-5b61-b6b0-ddc6438dc48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise smooth" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316140} {:answer/id #uuid "d8db2b4d-be1a-577e-9d71-586b8b3ff301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4a765d5-f9bc-5b61-b6b0-ddc6438dc48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise smooth" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316140} :answer-field/id #uuid "c367b66d-d706-58a4-8744-c9027f239869" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "779b25e7-e9f1-5970-81e6-c2457d778bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315791} {:answer/id #uuid "bb973c70-a9f5-5ed1-9595-2ee7f36dd4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316179} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc1e478-54e9-577d-b817-e82797475d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316357} {:answer/id #uuid "ea83f06e-8df8-5e52-bb5b-19418d0ece66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea83f06e-8df8-5e52-bb5b-19418d0ece66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316422} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1a1345d-5208-544e-96f2-59511c4c5a07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce2d6842-c273-5f28-8b8b-7bdf00107d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-343245" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-7{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-3,3).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-14x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-7{x}^{2}+4∼-17+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{252(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-14x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-17+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{252(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-3,3),$\n\n- continuous on $[-3,3),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-3)=F(3),$ if we extend the value at $x=3$ using the formula $F(x)=-7{x}^{2}+4.$\n\nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7{x}^{2}+4) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-17)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{252(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -14x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{252(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -14x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-84(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ -14x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{84(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0933967e-8a36-5c98-9978-af481d6e1c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315163} {:answer/id #uuid "6668d210-3666-5a78-bdab-b36c77b23f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315688} {:answer/id #uuid "c224d4a5-a69e-51bd-b87f-2a11fff0f518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c224d4a5-a69e-51bd-b87f-2a11fff0f518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316209} :answer-field/id #uuid "206ee1d4-18b6-5317-b71a-60ab4bb59aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308e0394-5c17-5c18-8ff0-e80da631f21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315392} {:answer/id #uuid "663577a8-6abe-5cfe-8679-56b730b9aecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315687} {:answer/id #uuid "abaf8f39-f4db-51da-95